    <div class="prose">
      <p>I'm Raven Whitley, founder of RaeAligned Strategic Services.</p>
      <p>My background is enterprise project and implementation leadership: program structure, keeping a lot of people working from the same plan, communications, training, and measuring whether any of it actually landed. Most recently I led logistics, training, communications, measurement, and senior-leader coordination for a large enterprise AI enablement program.</p>
      <p>That work taught me something I didn't expect. The failure modes are identical at every scale. A Fortune 500 program and a two-person business get stuck for the same reasons: the goal was never clearly stated, nobody owned the next step, and there was no system to catch it when the date slipped.</p>
      <p class="pull-inline">The scale changes. The missing pieces don't.</p>
      <p>RaeAligned exists to put those pieces in place for people who don't have a project management office: the shop owner who knows the system is broken, the person launching a service who doesn't know where to start, the organization with a big initiative and no one holding the shape of it.</p>
      <p>Some clients work with me for months. Some book one session and leave with a one-page plan. Both are real engagements.</p>
    </div>
